{"id":"000VN4","title":"Length and how you use it","author":"Procrastinathan","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-21T13:53:49+00:00","posted":"Heute, 13:53 Uhr","rules":"Length and how you use it\n\nThis is the first sudoku I have made, I hope you enjoy it!\n\nRules:\n\nNormal 9x9 sudoku rules apply.\n\nDefine the length of a digit to be the number of letters it has when written as a word in English.\n(e.g. one has 3 letters, so the length of the digit 1 is 3)\n\nLines: Digits along a red line must all have the same length.\n\nCages: The sum of digits enclosed within a cage must equal the sum of the lengths of the digits within that cage, digits may not repeat within a cage.\n\nSolve Online\n\nPuzzle:\n\nHappy Solving !!!","solutionCode":"Enter the digits of rows 5 and 8 with no spaces between them.","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/x68srlavs0","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/x68srlavs0","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-21T13:53:49+00:00"}